    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "02a24164e7915cd168d45fd71591ca569b316ddb3d6da31e0402de0f14ee3316",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-79efc77a-b889-42c3-95a7-4d1a8db6bd09",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, you meet your English-speaking guide for a tour of Medellín, the capital of Antioquia.\n\nYou visit the Museum of Antioquia and Plaza Botero, where Fernando Botero’s sculptures are on display. The tour also takes in the Palace of Culture and the Church of La Veracruz, two of the city’s well-known landmarks.\n\nYou then head to Comuna 13. Until relatively recently, it was considered one of Medellín’s most dangerous districts. Today it draws travellers from around the world for its graffiti, street art and cultural projects.\n\nThe last stop is the Castle Museum, built in 1930 and known for its art collection and gardens. After the tour, you return to your hotel to rest. In the evening, you can explore the city on your own, take a walk near the hotel or stay in."
    },
